<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20371" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hēlĭŏtrŏpĭum</span></b> ,
			ii, n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡλιοτρόπιον</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The plant turnsole</i>, <i>heliotrope</i>, <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 1, 46</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 2, 41,
				41, § 109</span></i>; <i><span class="en">22, 21, 29, §
			57</span></i>. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A precious stone with green and brown streaks</i>,
				<i>striped jasper</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 37,
				10, 60, § 165</span></i>.—Called also: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hēlĭŏtrŏpĭos</span></b> 
				(<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gemma</span></b> ),
					<i><span class="en">Mart. Cap. 1, § 75</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">heliotropius lapis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prisc. Perieg. 254</span></i>
			.</div>
